      "content": "Sure! Here are three distinct personality traits and backstories for each character to make them feel authentic:\n\n1. **Jamal** is a curious zookeeper who spends his free time sketching animal facts, often hiding a deep insecurity about his family expecting him to be a doctor. Despite his hectic schedule, he secretly volunteers at the local children's library, finding comfort in being listened to rather than just fixing problems.\n\n2. **Mr. Henderson** is stubbornly loyal to his bargain-hunting 60-year-old granddaughter, often bargaining over chick variety to keep her safe from scammers who target young mothers. He clings to the idea that his shop has a rare, old-fashioned charm compared to the \"real food\" at the supermarket, even though he admits he drives a beat-up car just to squeeze in five more customers daily.\n\n3. **Chloe** is sharp and fiercely protective of her animal rights friends, secretly maintaining a late-night diary in a locked diary that she shares with no one, including her inner circle of animal lovers. Though she dresses in a way that suggests she belongs anywhere in the boardroom, she is secretly horrified by corporate greed and constantly questions her own career choices while sipping a public kitchen",
